  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported). Income-statement items are CUMULATIVE from 1 January of the same year (as published in the bank's own First Quarter (Jan-Mar) unaudited interim financial statements), not discrete-quarter figures -- flagged via the _cumulative suffix, matching the convention already used in bank_financials/CITYBANK/quarterly and in this bank's own Q4 series' 'calculated_annual_minus_9m' handling. PDF is a pure scanned image (no text layer). OCR'd at 400 DPI. The printed 'Total operating income' line OCR'd as 14,871,216,499, which is exactly 3,000,000,000 more than both (a) the sum of the four income components and (b) 'Profit before provision' plus 'Total operating expenses' \u2014 both independently agreeing at 11,871,216,499, which is used instead (also independently confirmed: the FY2026 Q1 report's own Mar-2025 comparative column shows this same corrected figure, 11,871,216,499, exactly). Heavy provisioning (5,028.6m) against a 5,100.2m pre-provision profit left profit-before-tax at only 71.6m for the quarter, and a large net tax benefit (-813.5m) lifted net profit to 885.1m \u2014 both cross-checked via the PBT/tax/PAT identity and consistent with the FY2024/2025 sector-wide provisioning cycle. EPS OCR'd as '1.61' in one pass; the arithmetic value (net profit / current shares outstanding) is 1.01, which is used, and is corroborated by the comparative EPS figure (1.46 for Mar-2024) matching exactly between OCR passes and arithmetic.",
